{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791539347,"nonce":"V9BnZZhKUi5AbfpijFgxVpvgzeU=","title":"Measured TreeMotion after native renderer/polling fixes, rebuilt Ash application preset, macOS. The GC phase probe uses the real TreeMotion build/script, reports hl.Gc.stats() before UI and at 0.3/1/3/5/7 seconds, and runs two explicit diagnostic major collections at 7 seconds. Normal application behavior is unchanged.","message":"GC allocations (cumulative / current used blocks):\n- before UI: 0.58 / 0.66 MiB, identical in every arm\n- old LLVM threshold 250: 27.36 cumulative after motion, 12.69 current after normal idle cleanup, 12.03 after two majors\n- application threshold 10,000: 27.48 cumulative, 12.84 current, 12.16 after two majors\n- Cranelift only: 27.52 cumulative, 12.81 current, 12.13 after two majors\n- interpreter: 26.77 cumulative, 12.47 current, 11.88 after two majors\n\nFinalizers are being called:\n- application: 1,442 registered, 1,118 queued, 1,118 completed, 0 pending\n- Cranelift: 1,454 / 1,130 / 1,130 / 0\n- interpreter: 1,323 / 999 / 999 / 0\n- old 250: 1,448 / 1,124 / 1,124 / 0\nThe extra major collections find no additional dead finalizers and reclaim \u003c1 MiB of used GC blocks. No abandoned collections in these probes. External pressure in the GC report includes the synthetic 4 KiB per-finalizable-handle charge; it is not a measurement of native bytes owned by each handle.\n\nThe remaining memory has identifiable native owners. MallocStackLogging=lite + heap + malloc_history on TreeMotion with Cranelift only, after the diagnostic major collections:\n- AIR pipeline/optimizer cache roots: 50.10 MiB of live malloc allocations\n- SSA walker prepare/cache roots: 19.27 MiB\n- decoded program: 14.07 MiB\n- Cranelift-specific compilation/code malloc roots: 1.89 MiB (separate executable VM pages not included)\n- GPU/driver malloc roots: 7.41 MiB (GPU textures/VM mappings not included)\nThe heap census independently groups ~93.5 MiB under bytecode/AIR/interpreter/Cranelift leaf allocators. These are logical live allocation totals under instrumentation, not physical footprint: untouched GC reservations, VM regions and stack-logging overhead must be excluded from conclusions about RSS. The ~397 MiB GC side-table reservation is mostly untouched and is not ~397 MiB committed heap.\n\nRoot cause for the largest buckets remains existing Ash issue f60b855: OPTIMIZED retains Arc\u003cOptimized\u003e with IR and serialization per (findex, configuration); the SSA walker also retains its prepared IR copy, liveness and source/OSR maps. GC finalizers do not own or release these Rust caches. Releasing them needs to preserve live frames, source locations, OSR and retier construction. Existing 6fde0a9 covers remaining LLVM metadata; increasing Application's threshold is committed separately as 69f3fa3 (c3ee908).\n\nLocal artifacts in ashui:\n- .ashui/memory-comparison/application-103849/report.json (paired threshold comparison: mean 205.83 -\u003e 184.77 MiB)\n- .ashui/memory-comparison/gc-phases-104321/report.json\n- .ashui/memory-comparison/heap-104444/tree-heap.txt\n- .ashui/memory-comparison/heap-104444/tree-malloc_history.txt\n- .ashui/memory-comparison/heap-104444/malloc-attribution.json\n\nFinalizer diagnostics added behind ASH_GC_STATS; counters track registered/queued/completed/pending. Existing ash_std finalizer tests pass (4/4). This investigation does not establish that all components or scenes have no resource leaks; it excludes a finalizer backlog as the source of this TreeMotion gap.","files":null}]}